&lt;p&gt;12&sol;2005 - CMS clarified that bone marrow and peripheral blood stem cell transplantation is a process which includes mobilization, harvesting, and transplant of bone marrow or peripheral blood stem cells and the administration of high dose chemotherapy or radiotherapy prior to the actual transplant. When bone marrow or peripheral blood stem cell transplantation is covered, all necessary steps are included in coverage. When bone marrow or peripheral blood stem cell transplantation is non-covered, none of the steps are covered. Effective date 11&sol;28&sol;2005. Implementation date 01&sol;03&sol;2006. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;R45NCD.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 45&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 4173)&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;04&sol;2005 - Covered for primary AL amyloidosis when amyloid deposition in 2 or fewer organs and cardiac left ventricular ejection fraction greater than 45%. All forms of non-primary AL amyloidosis remain non-covered. Effective date 3&sol;15&sol;2005. Implementation date 5&sol;16&sol;2005. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;R32NCD.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 32&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 3797)&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;05&sol;2004 - Removed coding guidance. Coding guidance remains in the Claims Processing Manual. Effective date 7&sol;01&sol;2004. Implementation date 7&sol;06&sol;2004. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;R13NCD.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 13&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 3265)&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;04&sol;2003 - Removed reference to age as limitation on coverage of stem cell transplantation for patients with multiple myeloma. Effective date 10&sol;01&sol;2000. Implementation date 5&sol;9&sol;2003. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;R169CIM.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 169&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 2604)&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;11&sol;2000 - Removed age limitation for coverage of autologous stem cell transplantation for patients with multiple myeloma. Effective date 10&sol;1&sol;2000. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;AB00104.pdf&quot;&gt;PM AB-00-104&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 1375)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;08&sol;2000 - Covered for patients with multiple myeloma. Effective and implementation dates 10&sol;01&sol;2000. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;R125CIM.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 125&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 1002)&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;04&sol;1996 - Clarified that policy for bone marrow transplants applies to all types of stem cell transplants, and added multiple myeloma to conditions excluded from coverage. Effective date 05&sol;24&sol;1996. (TN 84)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
